data: {"text":"The 2000 G500 uses the M113 V8, a single-overhead-cam, all-aluminum engine with timing chains and two spark plugs per cylinder that produces 300 hp and 300 lb-ft of torque; the hosts call it reliable because it is simple, easy to work on, has cheap and globally available parts, and is known as the “Land Cruiser Killer” [1][2]."}

